== Notes ==
* If Call of Valor is used while a conjured creature is still active, the shout will dispel the creature and replace it with the summoned hero. The reverse can happen as well; if a summoned hero is active, a [[Skyrim:Conjure|Conjure]] spell will dispel the hero and replace it with the conjured creature. This even applies to summoning [[Skyrim:Durnehviir|Durnehviir]], as well, as he is considered a summoned creature: calling for Durnehviir's help will dispel the heroes of Sovngarde, and summoning a hero of Sovngarde will dispel Durnehviir.
* The heroes summoned by Call of Valor can be healed by restoration spells such as [[Skyrim:Healing Hands|Healing Hands]] and the shout allows one to keep the summoned hero indefinitely, unless another creature is summoned.
* It is not possible to have the [[Skyrim:Spectral Assassin|Spectral Assassin]] and the Hero of Sovngarde summon out together, even with the [[Skyrim:Twin Souls|Twin Souls]] perk. Summoning one after the other will relinquish the former. The same applies with the [[Skyrim:Arniel's Shade|Arniel's Shade]] [[Skyrim:Summon Arniel's Shade|summon]].
* If you happen to be in the path of the hero's Unrelenting Force shout, you will be ragdolled just as much as any enemy you were standing next to.

==Bugs==
{{Bug|Like [[Skyrim:Conjure|Conjure]] spells, the shout may be absorbed by any active [[Skyrim:Spell Absorption|Spell Absorption]] effects. If the shout is absorbed, a hero will not be summoned, but the shout's cooldown will still be triggered.|USKP|1.2.1}}

